            <c:note/>
            <c:pages>394b28</c:pages>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="AnTingshan1997">
            <c:pages>109-110, 128</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">An Tingshan briefly mentions the inscription.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">安廷山簡略提到了該銘文。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LiJingjie1997a">
            <c:pages>45</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Li Jingjie attributes the inscription to Seng’an Daoyi.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">李靜杰認為該銘文出自僧安道壹之手。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="ZhangZong1997">
            <c:pages>109</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Zhang Zong holds that this Buddha name is an allusion to Seng’an
                Daoyi’s name.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">張總認為該佛名暗示了僧安道壹的名字。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LaiFei2000b">
            <c:pages>8</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Lai Fei mentions the inscription.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">賴非提到了該銘文。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="ZhangZong2003a">
            <c:pages>16-17</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Zhang Zong refers to occurrences of this Buddha name in the printed
                    <hi rend="italic">
                    <foreign xml:lang="ja">Taishō</foreign>
                </hi> edition. He
                suggests that the name may have resonated with Seng’an Daoyi’s own name, conferring
                on him additional prestige.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">張總提到該佛名見於《大正藏》，並假設這個佛名也許和僧安道壹本人的名字相呼應，由此提高他的聲望。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="Kiriya2003a">
            <c:pages>71</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Kiriya holds that this Buddha name alludes to the name of Seng’an
                Daoyi and to the Chan practice of quieting the mind (<hi rend="italic">anxin</hi>
                <foreign xml:lang="zh">安心</foreign>).</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">桐谷征一認為該佛名暗指僧安道壹的名字以及禪修中的“安心”。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LaiFei2007">
            <c:note lang="en">Lai Fei gives the inscription’s location, its measurements and a
                transcription, and says that the three characters are well preserved. See also <ref type="biblio" target="LaiFei2000b">109</ref>.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">賴非提供了銘文的位置、測量數據及錄文，並說這三個字都保存良好。參見<ref type="biblio" target="LaiFei2000b">109</ref>。</c:note>
            <c:pages>28</c:pages>
        </c:ref>
